From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 01:31:12 +0200
Subject: phy: sun4i-usb: Don't force session end on dr_mode change when role
 is claimed

With the role switch claimed, id/vbus derive from usb_role and a
dr_mode change cannot affect phy0 routing, yet set_mode still forced an
id reprocess with a session end.  Each EHCI0/OHCI0 probe (usb_add_hcd
sets PHY_MODE_USB_HOST) thus bounced the running gadget session with a
1s vbus-off pulse during boot, delaying enumeration to ~6s and making
the device flap on the host.

Skip the force when the mode actually changed and a role is claimed.
An unchanged mode keeps forcing: sunxi_musb_recover() relies on that to
end the session for babble recovery.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c | 14 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -548,6 +548,20 @@ static int sun4i_usb_phy_set_mode(struct phy *_phy,
 	if (new_mode != data->dr_mode) {
 		dev_info(&_phy->dev, "Changing dr_mode to %d\n", new_mode);
 		data->dr_mode = new_mode;
+
+		/*
+		 * When a role switch consumer has claimed the port, id/vbus
+		 * are derived from usb_role and a dr_mode change cannot
+		 * affect the routing -- skip the forced session end.  The
+		 * EHCI0/OHCI0 probes set host mode on phy0 via
+		 * usb_add_hcd() and would otherwise each cause a spurious
+		 * 1s disconnect pulse of the running gadget session during
+		 * boot.  An *unchanged* mode still falls through below:
+		 * sunxi_musb_recover() calls set_mode with the current mode
+		 * specifically to force a session end.
+		 */
+		if (data->usb_role >= 0)
+			return 0;
 	}
 
 	data->id_det = -1; /* Force reprocessing of id */
-- 
Armbian

